{
  "name": "vector_light_door_aperture",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a727e phase 2, filmed: does the beam track the door's leaves as they slide, and what does tracking cost. Two hand-rolled sweeps over the same wooden door's swing, differing only in vector_light_door_aperture. Hand-rolled rather than TickLapse on purpose -- AdvanceTicks is a JUMP, so a door's own Tick() never runs under it, and the first cut of this film came back with the aperture pinned at 0 for every frame while still passing. SetTimeSpeed normal is what makes the door actually move. door_aperture_bakes is the number the performance claim rests on: rebakes per swing, which quantisation caps at steps+1 however slowly the door moves.",
